ite now works.** P9 commit `91c5c8cd` (\\\"feat(yang.php): P9 — the builtin surface\\n   slices\\\") deleted `php/str-write-error` and added `php/string-assign`, wired into `path-assign-at`\\n   (`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`). Focused walker probe:\\n   `<?php $s=\\\"ab\\\"; $s[0]=\\\"c\\\"; echo $s;` renders `\\\"cb\\\"`.\\n   - `test/yang/php/antlr/programs.cljc` `:string-offset-write` flipped from the G-str-offset-write\\n     refusal pin to the working expectation (`:out \\\"cb\\\"`, `:diag []`, `:uncaught`/`:gap` removed).\\n   - `test/yang/php/antlr/prelude_test.cljc` `array-path-assign-test` now pins\\n     `(php/echo (php/path-assign \\\"abc\\\" [0] \\\"x\\\"))` → `\\\"xbc\\\"`.\\n   - `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`: all 4 G-str-offset-write rows marked\\n     `closed 2026-11-04` citing `91c5c8cd`.\\n2. **strtoupper is a prelude builtin.** `builtins/supported` maps `\\\"strtoupper\\\"` to `php/bi-strtoupper`\\n   and `prelude/builtin-names` derives from that table, so no `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` warning is\\n   emitted and the call runs. `e2e_test.clj` `lowering-warnings-test` updated to no-warning + `\\\"A\\\"`.\\n3. **`$$a[0] = 1` now assigns through.** `base-location` (`lower.cljc`) locates a `Dollar`+`VarName`\\n   base as `{:var {:dynamic-name ...}}`, and `write-loc` writes a dynamic var with a path back via\\n   `dict-put!`. Focused walker probes: `<?php $$a[0] = 1;` lowers with no diagnostics (renders `\\\"\\\"`);\\n   `<?php $a = \\\"x\\\"; $x = [10, 20]; $$a[0] = 1; echo $x[0]; echo \\\",\\\"; echo $x[1];` renders `\\\"1,20\\\"`;\\n   `<?php $a = \\\"y\\\"; $$a[0] = 1; echo $y[0];` renders `\\\"1\\\"` (vivifies). So the engine resolves it as\\n   `${$a}[0]`. Refusals entry removed; new `variable-variable-offset-assign-test` pins `\\\"1,20\\\"`.\\n\\n## Laptop gates (all green)\\n\\n- `clojure -M:test -v yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/fixtures-on-the-walker-test\\n  -v .../lowering-warnings-test -v .../refusals-are-named-test\\n  -v .../variable-variable-offset-assign-test` → 4 tests, 557 assertions, 0 failures.\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test` → 33 tests, 373 assertions, 0 failures.\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` over the three touched test files → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\\n- No cljstyle runner is configured in this repo (`.cljstyle` present, no alias/CI invocation); edits\\n  match surrounding formatting. Full `e2e-test` namespace NOT run locally per the hard constraint.\\n\\n## Oracle: NOT performed on laptop (no docker/php) — seat oracle-check list for shiva\\n\\nPHP-truth assumed from the unambiguous documented behavior; the seat must confirm each on `php:8.3`\\nbefore landing (mark any doubt — none structural, but all three are oracle-unconfirmed):\\n\\n1. `php -r '$s=\\\"ab\\\"; $s[0]=\\\"c\\\"; echo $s;'` must print `cb`.\\n2. `php -r 'echo strtoupper(\\\"a\\\");'` must print `A`.\\n3. `php -r '$a = \\\"x\\\"; $x = [10, 20]; $$a[0] = 1; echo $x[0], \\\",\\\", $x[1];'` — engine prints `1,20`\\n   (i.e. `${$a}[0]` resolution); confirm Zend agrees, else the new pin's reading is wrong.\\n4. Seat gate: full `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.e2e-test` on shiva (includes the slow\\n   `fixtures-on-every-vm-test`, not run here).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '5010,5235p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-engineer-p1-followup.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.findings.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"           (php/take-rest acc l i nl)\\n           (if (<= (cmp (get l i) (get r j)) 0)\\n             (php/merge l r (+ i 1) j nl nr cmp (php/vconj acc (get l i)))\\n             (php/merge l r i (+ j 1) nl nr cmp (php/vconj acc (get r j)))))))]\\n    [php/msort\\n     (fn [xs cmp]\\n       (let [n (data/count xs)]\\n         (if (< n 2)\\n           xs\\n           (let [mid (get (integer/quot-rem n 2) 0)\\n                 l (php/msort (data/subvec xs 0 mid) cmp)\\n                 r (php/msort (data/subvec xs mid n) cmp)]\\n             (php/merge l r 0 0 (data/count l) (data/count r) cmp [])))))]\\n    [php/flag-cmp\\n     (fn [flag]\\n       (if (= flag 0)\\n         (fn [a b] (php/cmp a b))\\n         (if (= flag 1)\\n           (fn [a b] (php/cmp (php/to-float a) (php/to-float b)))\\n           (if (= flag 2)\\n             (fn [a b] (php/cmp-h (data/str-compare (php/to-string a) (php/to-string b)) 0))\\n             (php/throw-error\\n               \\\"Error\\\"\\n               (data/str-concat \\\"sort flag \\\" (integer/format flag)\\n                                \\\" is not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-sort-flags)\\\"))))))]\\n    [php/field-cmp\\n     ;; compare pairs on field `by` (0 key, 1 value), sign flips for r* variants\\n     (fn [by sign base]\\n       (fn [a b] (* sign (base (get a by) (get b by)))))]\\n    [php/user-cmp\\n     (fn [f]\\n       (let [warned (cell/new false)]\\n         (fn [a b]\\n           (let [r (php/call f (php/pair a b))]\\n             (if (= (php/kind r) :bool)\\n               (do (if (cell/get warned)\\n                     :php/null\\n                     (do (cell/set! warned true)\\n                         (php/warn 8192 \\\"usort(): Returning bool from comparison function is deprecated, return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero\\\")))\\n                   (if r\\n                     1\\n                     (if (> (php/to-int (php/call f (php/pair b a))) 0) -1 0)))\\n               (php/to-int r))))))]\\n    [php/rebuild\\n     (fn [sorted i n acc keep]\\n       (if (< i n)\\n         (let [it (get sorted i)]\\n           (php/rebuild sorted (+ i 1) n\\n                        (if keep\\n                          (php/array-set acc (get it 0) (get it 2))\\n                          (php/array-append acc (get it 2)))\\n                        keep))\\n         acc))]\\n    [php/sort-finish\\n     (fn [arr sorted keep]\\n       (let [out (php/rebuild sorted 0 (data/count sorted) (php/empty-array) keep)\\n             nx (get (php/arr-table arr) :next-index)]\\n         (php/out1 true\\n                   (if keep (if (nil? nx) out (php/with-next-index out nx)) out))))]\\n    [php/with-next-index\\n     (fn [out nx]\\n       (if (= (php/slot-kind out) :arr-handle)\\n         (let [c (get out :php/arr)\\n               st (cell/get c)]\\n           (do (cell/set! c (assoc st :value (assoc (get st :value) :next-index nx))) out))\\n         (assoc out :next-index nx)))]\\n    [php/triple (fn [a b c] (php/vconj (php/vconj (php/vconj [] a) b) c))]\\n    [php/do-sort\\n     (fn [name args by keep sign]\\n       (do (php/arity-between name args 1 2 \\\"at least 1\\\")\\n           (let [arr (php/arg-array (get args 0) name 1 \\\"array\\\")\\n                 flag (if (> (data/count args) 1) (php/to-int (get args 1)) 0)\\n                 cmp (php/field-cmp by sign (php/flag-cmp flag))]\\n             (php/sort-finish arr\\n                              (php/msort (php/pairs arr 0 (php/array-count arr) []) cmp)\\n                              keep))))]\\n    [php/do-usort\\n     (fn [name args by keep]\\n       (do (php/arity-between name args 2 2 \\\"exactly 2\\\")\\n           (let [arr (php/arg-array (get args 0) name 1 \\\"array\\\")\\n                 cmp (php/field-cmp by 1 (php/user-cmp (php/callable-fn (get args 1))))]\\n             (php/sort-finish arr\\n                              (php/msort (php/pairs arr 0 (php/array-count arr) []) cmp)\\n                              keep))))]\\n    [php/bi-sort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"sort\\\" args 1 false 1))]\\n    [php/bi-rsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"rsort\\\" args 1 false -1))]\\n    [php/bi-asort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"asort\\\" args 1 true 1))]\\n    [php/bi-arsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"arsort\\\" args 1 true -1))]\\n    [php/bi-ksort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"ksort\\\" args 0 true 1))]\\n    [php/bi-krsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \\\"krsort\\\" args 0 true -1))]\\n    [php/bi-usort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \\\"usort\\\" args 1 false))]\\n    [php/bi-uasort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \\\"uasort\\\" args 1 true))]\\n    [php/bi-uksort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \\\"uksort\\\" args 0 true))]\\n\\n    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- unit\\n    [php/bi-set-exception-handler\\n     (fn [args]\\n       (let [old (cell/get php.rt/exception-handler)]\\n         (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handlers\\n                        (php/vconj (cell/get php.rt/exception-handlers) old))\\n             (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler (get args 0))\\n             old)))]\\n    [php/bi-restore-exception-handler\\n     ;; back to the handler in force before the last `set_exception_handler`\\n     (fn [args]\\n       (let [stack (cell/get php.rt/exception-handlers)\\n             n (data/count stack)]\\n         (do (if (= n 0)\\n               (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler :php/null)\\n               (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler (get stack (- n 1)))\\n                   (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handlers (php/args-prefix stack (- n 1) 0 []))))\\n             true)))]\\n    [php/handle-uncaught\\n     ;; the user exception handler takes an uncaught throwable; the script then ends\\n     (fn [exc]\\n       (let [h (cell/get php.rt/exception-handler)]\\n         (if (= exc :php/null)\\n           exc\\n           (if (= h :php/null)\\n             exc\\n             (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler :php/null)\\n                 (php/try (fn [] (do (php/call-value h (php/vconj [] exc)) :php/null))\\n                          (fn [e] e)\\n                          (fn [] :php/null)))))))]\\n    [php/run-main\\n     ;; the unit root: output, response records, diagnostics and any uncaught error.\\n     ;; The operational fatal escapes past everything through php/root-fatal;\\n     ;; exit escapes past handlers and finally blocks through php/root-exit\\n     ;; and its status is preserved through shutdown\\n     (fn [body]\\n       (do (cell/set! php.rt/out [[]])\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/ctx (php/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/response [])\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/headers-sent false)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/status 200)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/exit-status :php/null)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/in-shutdown false)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/fatal-escape :php/null)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/exit-escape :php/null)\\n           (cell/set! php.rt/shutdown-escape :php/null)\\n           (let [result (fn [exc]\\n                          (let [out (data/str-join \\\"\\\" (get (cell/get php.rt/out) 0))\\n                                response (cell/get php.rt/response)]\\n                            (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :php/out out)\\n                                                 :php/diag (cell/get php.rt/diag))\\n                                          :php/uncaught\\n                                          (if (= exc :php/null) nil (php/snapshot-exc exc)))\\n                                   :php/response\\n                                   (if (= out \\\"\\\")\\n                                     response\\n                                     (php/vconj response (assoc {} :php.response/body out))))))\\n                 fatal (fn [message] (assoc (result :php/null) :php/fatal message))\\n                 v (php/call-terminal\\n                    (fn [fesc]\\n                      (do (cell/set! php.rt/fatal-escape fesc)\\n                          (php/call-terminal\\n                           (fn [eesc]\\n                             (do (cell/set! php.rt/exit-escape eesc)\\n                                 (let [exc0 (php/try (fn [] (do (body) :php/null))\\n                                                     (fn [e] e)\\n                                                     (fn [] :php/null))]\\n                                   (if (= true (get exc0 :php/operational))\\n                                     (fesc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :php/terminal :fatal)\\n                                                        :php/operational true)\\n                                                  :message (get exc0 :message)))\\n                                     (php/pair :normal exc0)))))))))]\\n             (if (= (get v :php/terminal) :fatal)\\n               (fatal (get v :message))\\n               (let [ex (cell/get php.rt/exit-status)\\n                     exc0 (if (= (get v :php/terminal) :exit) :php/null (get v 1))\\n                     exc1 (if (= ex :php/null) (php/handle-uncaught exc0) :php/null)\\n                     s (php/call-terminal\\n                        (fn [sesc]\\n                          (do (cell/set! php.rt/shutdown-escape sesc)\\n                              (cell/set! php.rt/in-shutdown true)\\n                              (let [exc2 (php/try (fn [] (do (php/shutdown!) :php/null))\\n                                                  (fn [e] e)\\n                                                  (fn [] :php/null))]\\n                                (if (= true (get exc2 :php/operational))\\n                                  (php/root-fatal (get exc2 :message))\\n                                  (php/pair :normal exc2))))))\\n                     ;; the drain of unclosed buffers, outside the shutdown\\n                     ;; escape: an exit during shutdown aborts the sequence\\n                     ;; past this point, so the drain must run here, on every\\n                     ;; path that reaches the exit status; the operational\\n                     ;; fatal escapes past everything and never reaches here\\n                     ex2 (do (php/drain-buffers!) (cell/get php.rt/exit-status))\\n                     st (if (= ex2 :php/null) ex ex2)\\n                     exc2 (if (= (get s :php/terminal) :exit) :php/null (get s 1))\\n                     e (if (= exc1 :php/null) exc2 exc1)\\n                     r (result (if (= e :php/null) :php/null e))]\\n                 (if (= st :php/null) r (assoc r :php/status st)))))))]])\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private builtins\\n  \\\"The functions `php/init!` registers: PHP name to prelude definition,\\n   derived from `builtins/supported`, the one table.\\\"\\n  (mapv (fn [[nm {:keys [prelude]}]] [nm prelude]) (sort-by key builtins/supported)))\\n\\n\\n(def builtin-names\\n  \\\"The lower-cased names of the functions `php/init!` registers.\\\"\\n  (set (map first builtins)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private seed-classes\\n  \\\"The builtin classes and interfaces `php/init!` seeds: [name kind parent\\n   interfaces final?], parents before children (P4 owns the rest of the\\n   builtin descriptor skeletons).\\\"\\n  [[\\\"Traversable\\\" :interface nil []] [\\\"Iterator\\\" :interface nil [\\\"Traversable\\\"]]\\n   [\\\"IteratorAggregate\\\" :interface nil [\\\"Traversable\\\"]] [\\\"ArrayAccess\\\" :interface nil []]\\n   [\\\"Countable\\\" :interface nil []] [\\\"Stringable\\\" :interface nil []]\\n   [\\\"JsonSerializable\\\" :interface nil []] [\\\"UnitEnum\\\" :interface nil []]\\n   [\\\"BackedEnum\\\" :interface nil [\\\"UnitEnum\\\"]] [\\\"Throwable\\\" :interface nil [\\\"Stringable\\\"]]\\n   [\\\"stdClass\\\" :class nil []] [\\\"Closure\\\" :class nil [] true]\\n   [\\\"Generator\\\" :class nil [\\\"Iterator\\\"] true]\\n   [\\\"Exception\\\" :class nil [\\\"Throwable\\\"]] [\\\"Error\\\" :class nil [\\\"Throwable\\\"]]\\n   [\\\"ErrorException\\\" :class \\\"Exception\\\" []] [\\\"JsonException\\\" :class \\\"Exception\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"RuntimeException\\\" :class \\\"Exception\\\" []] [\\\"LogicException\\\" :class \\\"Exception\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"TypeError\\\" :class \\\"Error\\\" []] [\\\"ValueError\\\" :class \\\"Error\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"ArithmeticError\\\" :class \\\"Error\\\" []] [\\\"DivisionByZeroError\\\" :class \\\"ArithmeticError\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"ArgumentCountError\\\" :class \\\"TypeError\\\" []] [\\\"UnhandledMatchError\\\" :class \\\"Error\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"InvalidArgumentException\\\" :class \\\"LogicException\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"DomainException\\\" :class \\\"LogicException\\\" []] [\\\"LengthException\\\" :class \\\"LogicException\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"OutOfRangeException\\\" :class \\\"LogicException\\\" []]\\n   [\\\"BadFunctionCallException\\\" :class \\\"LogicException\\\" []]\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-05\\nCoding-Agent: muse (muse-spark, laptop)\\nTask: Round-A follow-ups from the architect's landing review — the shutdown\\noperational-exc2 fallback and the buffer-drain placement (prelude.cljc)\\n\\n## Changes (src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc, one file)\\n\\n1. Shutdown operational-exc2 fallback: `(fesc ...)` -> `(php/root-fatal\\n   (get exc2 :message))` (run-main, ex-:5189). The old call was\\n   literally out of scope: the `fesc` lambda closes over the body-exit\\n   `call-terminal`, while the exc2 site sits inside the sibling\\n   shutdown `call-terminal` (`fn [sesc]`), so `fesc` there is a free\\n   variable. Independent include-boundary regression confirmed on the\\n   base: bundled-prelude-is-closed-test FAIL +\\n   module-spec-declares-every-free-name-test ERROR (core/module-spec\\n   refuses the undeclared free name); both pass after the fix.\\n   Operational semantics preserved: root-fatal still escapes through\\n   the fatal continuation, bypassing guest handlers, returns and\\n   finalizers.\\n2. Buffer drain moved outside the shutdown escape. `php/shutdown!`\\n   no longer drains (comment updated); run-main drains once on the\\n   exit path via `ex2 (do (php/drain-buffers!)\\n   (cell/get php.rt/exit-status))`, which runs on every path that\\n   reaches the exit status — normal and exit-during-shutdown — while\\n   the operational fatal escapes past it (bypass intact, buffers\\n   discarded on fatal per PHP semantics).\\n\\n## REPL-level checks (all observed)\\n\\n- Linked module publishes clean: free names are only\\n  yang.call/{eligible?,entry,invoke,invoke-with} (declared via\\n  requires); no `fesc` stray; module-spec builds (php, 842 exports,\\n  53 primitives).\\n- Drain case (ob_start + shutdown fn echoing S + exit 3 + echo A):\\n  out \\\"AS\\\", status 3, no fatal. Before the fix the escape skipped\\n  the drain and rendered buffer zero.\\n- Fatal bypass: shutdown fn raising operational reports fatal\\n  \\\"boom\\\", out \\\"\\\", no status, no drain crash.\\n\\n## Gates (laptop-legal)\\n\\n- clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test: 33 tests,\\n  373 assertions, 1 failure (array-path-assign-test, pre-existing —\\n  fails identically on the unmodified base, which additionally shows\\n  the closed + module-spec failures above).\\n- clojure -M:test + finalization-test + exceptions-test: 42 tests,\\n  407 assertions, same single pre-existing failure, 0 errors.\\n- clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc: 0 errors,\\n  0 warnings.\\n- cljstyle: not runnable on this laptop (no cljstyle alias/binary);\\n  not run. No e2e/slow/subsystem suites run (laptop rule).\\n\\n## Escalations\\n\\nNone. One residual: array-path-assign-test (string-offset-write gap\\nmessage) fails on base and tree alike; owned elsewhere.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:27:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ls /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/git /opt/homebrew/bin/git; rg --files collab/orch-lane | rg 'retro|review|architect' | tail -60; rg -n 'verdict 3|stale slow|fesc|P9 section' collab/orch-lane --glob '*findings*' --glob '*report*' | tail -65\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/