ws\\\\\\\\n1770\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n1771\\\\\\\\t### 10.1 Value encoding (runtime profile data)\\\\\\\\n1772\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n1773\\\\\\\\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n1774\\\\\\\\t| PHP type        | Representation                                             |\\\\\\\\n1775\\\\\\\\t+=================+============================================================+\\\\\\\\n1776\\\\\\\\t| int             | exact integer within `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (C3 carriers; on    |\\\\\\\\n1777\\\\\\\\t|                 | the JavaScript host a value past 2^53 is a `BigInt`        |\\\\\\\\n1778\\\\\\\\t|                 | carrier); an operation's overflow demotes to float         |\\\\\\\\n1779\\\\\\\\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n1780\\\\\\\\t| float           | Jing float64 content (carrier on the JavaScript host); one |\\\\\\\\n1781\\\\\\\\t|                 | NaN; `-0.0` preserved; `INF`                               |\\\\\\\\n1782\\\\\\\\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n1783\\\\\\\\t| string          | **byte string**: a host string whose every char is one     |\\\\\\\\n1784\\\\\\\\t|                 | byte 0 to 255 (a latin-1 carrier of the bytes); source     |\\\\\\\\n1785\\\\\\\\t|                 | literals contribute their UTF-8 bytes; `strlen` counts     |\\\\\\\\n1786\\\\\\\\t|                 | bytes; output writes the bytes raw; `mb_*` is a separate   |\\\\\\\\n1787\\\\\\\\t|                 | slice over this representation (owner decision B8.2)       |\\\\\\\\n1788\\\\\\\\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n1789\\\\\\\\t| bool            | host boolean                                               |\\\\\\\\n1790\\\\\\\\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n1791\\\\\\\\t| null            | `:php/nu