1389\\t\\n  1390\\tReading `yang/php.cljc` confirms the audit: it has no cells (assignment is\\n  1391\\tlexical rebinding, so `$x = 1; $f = function() use ($x) {...}; $x = 2` and\\n  1392\\tevery loop-carried mutation are wrong except the single-threaded-variable\\n  1393\\tspecial case `for-threaded-var`), no arrays, no strings beyond literals, no\\n  1394\\t`echo` or output, no classes, references, null semantics or coercion, a\\n  1395\\tZ-combinator per function and per loop, type hints parsed and dropped, `-10;`\\n  1396\\tfolded into a literal, and PHP `null` lowered to host `nil`. Its tokenizer has\\n  1397\\tno modes (no HTML, no heredoc, no `<?=`). Replacing only its parser would keep\\n  1398\\tevery semantic defect. **Ruling: replace.** Nothing of the legacy lowering is\\n  1399\\treused; the Z-combinator encoding is superseded by self-applied `:loop`-marked\\n  1400\\tlambdas with cells, which also makes safepoints and tail marks work.\\n  1401\\t\\n  1402\\tMigration mechanics (the F2 pattern):\\n  1403\\t\\n  1404\\t- The ANTLR frontend is installed in `yin.repl.frontends/standard` as a\\n  1405\\t  new revision of `:yang/php` (the compiler frontend keeps its revision\\n  1406\\t  during the migration window; `[id revision]` pins either), with no\\n  1407\\t  fallback.\\n  1408\\t- Every program in `test/yang/php_test.clj` is re-expressed in the new corpus,\\n  1409\\t  with expectations corrected where the legacy was wrong (`null` is\\n  1410\\t  `:php/null`, not `nil`).\\n  1411\\t- The browser demo `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs`\\n  1412\\t  compiles editable PHP synchronously in CLJS with the legacy frontend, while\\n  1413\\t  the local ANTLR parser is JVM-only until a Dart helper exists (amended\\n  1414\\t  2026-10-17: PHP has Java and JavaScript helpers upstream; per-target helper\\n  1415\\t  availability decides the host matrix, `yang.antlr.md` 4.2). The demo moves to **checked-in CST packets**\\n  1416\\t  for its sample programs (generated by a JVM script, the `dht-import-v1.edn`\\n  1417\\t  pattern), lowered and run parserless in the browser; editable PHP source in\\n  1418\\t  the demo is dropped, or routed to a configured parser service when one\\n  1419\\t  exists (owner decision B8.9). `src/dev/subsystems.edn` is a one-line\\n  1420\\t  retarget.\\n  1421\\t- The compiler revision of `:yang/php` retires at P8 (implementation\\n  1422\\t  deleted, no shim; the repository has no backward-compatibility\\n  1423\\t  obligation) once the demo retarget has landed and the corpus covers the\\n  1424\\t  compiler's programs (owner decision B8.6).\\n  1425\\t\\n  1426\\tWhat stays refused after migration: `goto`; return by reference (corner C7);\\n  1427\\t`declare(encoding)`; `__halt_compiler`; `eval` until its slice; `$$` and\\n  1428\\t`extract` until the dynamic-scope slice; extension surfaces (`ext/*`: PDO,\\n   302\\t            \\\"Cannot use float as default value for parameter $x of type int\\\"]\\n   303\\t           [\\\"<?php function f(int $x = 'bad') {}\\\"\\n   304\\t            \\\"Cannot use string as default value for parameter $x of type int\\\"]\\n   305\\t           [\\\"<?php switch (1) { default: echo 1; default: echo 2; }\\\"\\n   306\\t            \\\"Switch statements may only contain one default clause\\\"]\\n   307\\t           [\\\"<?php switch (1): default: echo 1; case 2: break; default: echo 2; endswitch;\\\"\\n   308\\t            \\\"Switch statements may only contain one default clause\\\"]\\n   309\\t           [\\\"<?php function f() { switch (1) { default: break; default: break; } }\\\"\\n   310\\t            \\\"Switch statements may only contain one default clause\\\"]\\n   311\\t           [\\\"<?php echo $a[];\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   312\\t           [\\\"<?php $a[] += 1;\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   313\\t           [\\\"<?php $a[]++;\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   314\\t           [\\\"<?php $a[] ??= 1;\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   315\\t           [\\\"<?php echo $a[0][] ?? 1;\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   316\\t           [\\\"<?php echo isset($a[]);\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for reading\\\"]\\n   317\\t           [\\\"<?php unset($a[]);\\\" \\\"Cannot use [] for unsetting\\\"]]]\\n   318\\t    (let [{:keys [diagnostics]} (h/run-php source)\\n   319\\t          d (first diagnostics)]\\n   320\\t      (is (= :yang.php/compile-error (:yang.php/diagnostic d)) source)\\n   321\\t      (is (str/includes? (str (:message d)) fragment) source))))\\n   322\\t\\n   323\\t\\n   324\\t(deftest lowering-warnings-test\\n   325\\t  (testing \\\"a prelude builtin lowers with no warning and runs\\\"\\n   326\\t    (let [{:keys [ast warnings]} (h/lower-program \\\"<?php echo strtoupper(\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\");\\\")]\\n   327\\t      (is (some? ast))\\n   328\\t      (is (empty? warnings))\\n   329\\t      (testing \\\"and the call runs\\\"\\n   330\\t        (is (= \\\"A\\\" (h/run-walker \\\"<?php echo strtoupper(\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\");\\\"))))))\\n   331\\t  (testing \\\"a unit that declares the function, or a prelude builtin, does not\\\"\\n   332\\t    (is (empty? (:warnings (h/lower-program\\n   333\\t                             \\\"<?php function strtoupper($s) { return $s; } echo STRTOUPPER(\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\");\\\"))))\\n   334\\t    (is (empty? (:warnings (h/lower-program \\\"<?php echo strlen(\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\");\\\"))))\\n   335\\t    (is (empty? (:warnings (h/lower-program \\\"<?php echo not_a_php_function(1);\\\")))))\\n   336\\t  (testing \\\"continue aimed at a switch is a break and says so\\\"\\n   337\\t    (let [{:keys [warnings]}\\n   338\\t          (h/lower-program \\\"<?php for (;;) { switch (1) { case 1: continue; } break; }\\\")]\\n   339\\t      (is (= [:yang.php/compile-warning] (mapv :yang.php/diagnostic warnings))))\\n   340\\t    (is (= \\\"ab\\\" (h/run-walker \\\"<?php switch (1) { case 1: echo \\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\"; continue; e