at is a working bearer reference by design); verdict: retain the two operations, rule for a generic non-fatal authentication effect reusing the engine's existing authentic-ref? (engine.cljc:331), with five rules (strict explicit resolution; runtime authentication in ordinary application; authentication ≠ authorization per the :2120 pin; bearer copies retain behavior; static specialization is optimization-not-semantics). (2) The owner asked what \\\"authentication effect\\\" means; seat grounded it in the codebase: the cell module is an effect language (pure constructors + engine interpreter, module.cljc:378); authentic? = a fourth constructor + one interpreter case returning (authentic-ref? state :cell/ref ...) non-fatally — the query voice of the predicate that today only speaks as check-ref!'s fatal gate. Owner: \\\"oh i see. monadic effect ... ok. i like this idea. lets go with your recommendation\\\" — RULING ACCEPTED. (3) Ruling-of-record written (collab/yang-clojure/1794330000000-architect-cell-ref-ruling-of-record.md): the seven rules incl. scope decisions (entry-key policy OUT — rule 7; the bag clarification: storage changes nothing, the authentication query at the call decides) + required §8.10 documentation + the acceptance battery. (4) r5 dispatched to glm-5.3 (the owner's lane for this unit): the two scoped VM hunks, routing consults authentic? (shape = cheap pre-filter for WHEN to ask, never decides meaning), astra's reconciliation checklist binding (call.cljc:23 _descriptor, clojure.cljc:1245/1403/1458, ts prelude:135 + lower:1167, py prelude:1033, php prelude:4229), the collision-literal + bearer-copy + exposure-probe regressions, the docs. (5) BLAST-RADIUS ANALYSIS for the owner (grounded by grep): VM additive only (no vocabulary pins exist; state/protocol unchanged; the boolean oracle leaks nothing the fatal check didn't); the shared _descriptor definition is the CONTAINMENT mechanism (fix once, all convention frontends inherit); shape-routing sweep