`_frame`/WITH_META at lines 501–511.\\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-18-[Omitted long context line]\\ncollab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-19-- Plan sentence: \\\"Reject malformed CBOR, unknown tags or named wrappers outside this profile… Validate tag/name/payload shapes before any lossy host conversion\\\" (Encoding contract). A J1 implementer mirroring the corpus taxonomy has no ruling to mirror.\\ncollab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-20-- Smallest fix: rule the metadata map must be bare — in `_frame`'s WITH_META branch, after `m = to_node(p.value[0])`, raise `Refusal(\\\"malformed-frame\\\", \\\"metadata map itself carries metadata\\\")` when `\\\"meta\\\" in m`; add one decode-refusal fixture (e.g. `meta/decode-meta-with-own-meta`); record the ruling under A3/A10. This keeps \\\"one value has one metadata map\\\" consistent with `meta/decode-nested-with-meta`.\\n--\\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-44-| # | Corpus reading supported by the plan? | My ruling | Freeze risk |\\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-45-|---|---|---|---|\\ncollab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-46-| A1 | Yes — plan says tag 27 followed by \\\"exactly `[name-string, payload]`\\\"; flattened IANA form correctly `malformed-frame`. The `:on-unknown-record` note matches the work package's stale-plan correction. | Confirm. | Safe (bytes pinned by plan text) |\\ncollab/1790023590463-ref-review-qwen.findings.md-47-| A2 | Yes — plan: \\\"Frozen fixtures define the remaining Boring mappings for sets\\\". Cited hex `d90102820102` verified present at `test/dao/stream/cbor_test.cljc:62` (Boring-produced). | Confirm tag 258, definite array, bytewise sort; J1 must still confirm Boring 0.1.30 canonical emits it (README already says so). | Freezes bytes; strong prior art |\\ncollab/1790023590463-ref-revi